            <td>{c.meaning}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What are the seven quality management principles behind ISO 9001?</h2>
  <p>
    ISO’s companion brochure to the ISO 9000 family, "Quality management principles: your foundation
    for success," sets out seven principles that underpin ISO 9001 in both the 2015 and 2026 editions. They
    predate ISO 9001:2026, and give useful context for why clauses like leadership, improvement
    and evidence-based decision-making exist in the standard at all.
  </p>
  <ul>
    {principles.map((p) => (
      <li><strong>{p.name}.</strong> {p.body}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>How does Obel MS help with ISO 9001:2026 document control?</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/product/external-document-control">External Document Control</a> is built around clause 7.5 of
    ISO 9001, in both the 2015 and 2026 editions, since the underlying document control requirement is
    unchanged in substance. Every supplier certificate you upload is auto-filed by supplier, manufacturer and
    product, its status is worked out automatically as Active, Expiring soon, Expired or No expiry set, and
    every upload, approval and new version is recorded in a full audit trail you can hand an auditor directly.
  </p>
  <p>
    For the corrective action side of a quality management system, <a href="/product/workflow-manager">Workflow
    Manager</a> gives you a standard Nonconformance template with built-in effectiveness verification, so a
    nonconformance is logged, closed out and checked, with every stage of that process recorded in
